The `as TestStatusValue` cast is unsafe and can cause a runtime TypeError. If a status entry in `allStatuses` carries one of the new values (`status-value:new`, `status-value:modified`, `status-value:affected`) for the component-test or a11y type ID, then `statusValueToStoryIdsMap[status.value as TestStatusValue]` resolves to `undefined` (the key doesn't exist in the map), and calling `.push()` on it throws. A type assertion doesn't add a runtime guard—it only silences TypeScript. Replace the cast with an explicit membership check before pushing:
```ts
if (status.value in statusValueToStoryIdsMap) {
  statusValueToStoryIdsMap[status.value as TestStatusValue].push(status.storyId);
}
```
